            "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HUpniZTWUAArDuh.jpg?name=small",
            "width": 1024
          }
        ],
        "name": "Eva Fo𝕏 🦊 Claudius Nero's Legion",
        "text": "Jensen Huang once admitted that when NVIDIA unveiled its first AI supercomputer, nobody wanted it. Not a single purchase order.\n\nExcept for Elon Musk.\n\n\"He goes, 'You know what? I have a company that could really use this.'\"\n\nBut then came the twist: it was a nonprofit😂😂 The machine cost $300,000, and Jensen thought the odds of getting paid were \"approximately zero.\" He delivered it anyway, driving it to San Francisco himself in 2016 to a room full of researchers who turned out to be OpenAI.\n\nElon saw the value of AI computing when the whole world couldn't understand it. He's done it again and again, spotting the future years before everyone else, then backing it with action instead of words.",
        "url": "https://x.com/EvaFox/status/2110613332705075700",
        "verified": true,
        "verified_type": "individual"
      },
